<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  One day of the grocery store, ending when the last customer has left (PRO: ProcessFlow, closes).

  The same store as process-flow-checkout.xml (shopping delay, a group of lanes joined by queue length, checkout time by basket, hourly arrival rates; clock in
  minutes, the store open for 840), run for a single day: closes="840" stops external arrivals at minute 840, the customers already inside finish shopping and checkout,
  and when the last one has left the model ENDS by itself (an end of data, not an error), whatever count the run asks for. Grind reports it:
  "[the model ended: ... every customer has left after external arrivals stopped at clock time 840]".
  Output is the event log (output="events"), so the state at closing can be read off it. Output columns, 8 per row: 0 clock time (minutes), 1 customer number, 2 station
  (0 the shop, 1 to N the lanes), 3 event type (0 arrive, 1 start, 2 finish, 3 exit), 4 customers waiting at that station after the event, 5 servers busy there, 6 customers
  in the whole store after the event, 7 the number of items.

  To run it:        grind with a count of 200000 on samples/pro/process-flow-checkout-day.xml        (it stops by itself after about 5,000 events); set the lanes with the declare "lanes"
  What to look for: the customers in the lanes at closing are the sum, over the lane stations, of the "queue" value on each lane's last row at or before minute 840;
                    the customers in the store are "inSystem" on the last row at or before 840. Measured over 40 days (seeds 1 to 40): with 4 lanes 40.9 customers are waiting
                    in the lanes at closing and 54.5 are in the store; with 5 or 6 lanes none are waiting in a lane and 11.3 are in the store (all still shopping). Overtime,
                    the time from 840 to the last row, is about 72 minutes with 5 lanes or more, set by the last shoppers.
-->
<dataset columns="time, customer, station, type, queue, busy, inSystem, items" seed="20261014">
  <definitions>
    <declare name="lanes" value="6"/>
  </definitions>
  <root node="Store"/>
  <nodes>
    <Exponential name="Gap" lambda="1.0"/>
    <Lognormal name="Basket" mu="2.2" sigma="0.9"/>
    <Calculate name="Items" expression="y[0] = ceil(x[0])"><input name="Basket"/></Calculate>
    <Gamma name="ShopFactor" shape="4" scale="0.25"/>
    <Gamma name="PaceFactor" shape="8.16" scale="0.12254901960784313"/>
    <ProcessFlow name="Store" stations="Shop:inf, Lane[${lanes}]:1" entry="Shop" routing="Shop>Lane:1" output="events" closes="840"
                 attributes="items" serviceScale="Shop: 4 + 0.8 * items; Lane: 0.9 + 0.1 * items"
                 rate="0:0.6667, 60:1.0, 120:1.3333, 180:1.6667, 240:2.0, 300:1.6667, 360:1.3333, 420:1.5, 480:2.1667, 540:2.6667, 600:2.3333, 660:1.6667, 720:1.1667, 780:0.6667, 840:0"
                 ratePeriod="1440">
      <input name="Gap" role="arrival"/>
      <input name="Items" role="entity"/>
      <input name="ShopFactor" role="service.Shop"/>
      <input name="PaceFactor" role="service.Lane"/>
    </ProcessFlow>
  </nodes>
</dataset>
